# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are documented here.

## [0.1.0] - 2026-07-30

Initial public release.

### Added
- Fail-closed policy engine (`policy_engine.py`) — YAML-configured rules
  across three tiers (approve / log / block).
- Behavioral audit schema (`audit_schema.py`).
- Anonymization layer for sharing usage data (`anonymizer.py`).
- Aggregated dataset export to CSV/JSONL (`aggregated_dataset.py`).
- End-to-end example (`complete_flow.py`).
- Automated test suite (`test_policy_engine.py`), 9 tests, no external
  dependencies beyond `pyyaml`.
- `pip`-installable via `pyproject.toml`.
- `GETTING_STARTED.md` with a non-trading example.
- `SECURITY.md` vulnerability disclosure policy.

### Fixed (from internal audit before this release)
- Combined exposure check: a new order was checked in isolation against
  the contract cap, missing the case where existing open contracts plus
  a new order together exceed it.
- `increase_size` had the same gap for agents adding to an already-open
  position.
- Trading window check didn't support windows crossing midnight.
- SQL table name was interpolated without validation (allowlist added).
- Postgres connections had no timeout.
- Anthropic API calls had no retry for transient network errors.